## Risk Assessment

### Low Risk
- Steps 1, 2: Moving buttons to toolbar (pure addition)
- Step 5: Passing store prop (pure addition)
- Step 7: Cleanup (removing unused state)

### Medium Risk
- Step 3: Adding Speed/Seed controls (requires store integration)
- Step 4: Layout refactoring (CSS complexity, may need iteration)

### Higher Risk
- Step 6: Removing Transport (destructive change, must verify all functionality migrated)

## Rollback Strategy

Each step is atomic and can be reverted via git:
```bash
# Revert specific files
git checkout HEAD -- <file>

# Revert entire commit
git revert <commit-hash>
```

If issues arise during Step 6, the Transport component can be temporarily re-added while debugging.

## Post-Implementation

### Documentation Updates Needed
- Update PLAYERTIME.md with new architecture
- Document consolidated control layout
- Update any screenshots showing old layout

### Future Enhancements
- Add Player.setSpeed() method if not present
- Consider adding time display format options (ms vs s)
- Consider adding keyboard shortcuts for player controls
- Timeline metadata generation (see STATUS item #5 - separate task)

## Completion Criteria

All steps completed successfully when:
1. All buttons/controls migrated to new locations
2. Transport component completely removed
3. All tests passing
4. No regression in existing functionality
5. Visual polish complete (proper spacing, alignment)
6. Code is clean (no dead code, proper types)

